This product includes a TypeScript port of LiteParse
(https://github.com/run-llama/liteparse, tag crates-v2.21.2): the ocria-nano
OCR engine, the OCR merge, grid projection, the learned table and layout
model's decoding, markdown layout and output formatting. LiteParse is
Copyright LlamaIndex, Inc., licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The ported files say so in their headers.

The PDF entry (`ppu-ocria-nano/pdf`) ships pdfium compiled to WebAssembly: the patched
pdfium of run-llama/pdfium-binaries (release chromium/8172, pdfium 160.0.8172.0), linked
here with emscripten 3.1.72 (scripts/pdfium/build.sh). pdfium is Copyright The PDFium
Authors. The licenses of pdfium, of the pdfium-binaries build and of the libraries it
contains (among them FreeType, ICU, libjpeg-turbo, libpng, OpenJPEG and zlib) are in the
package's `pdf/licenses/` folder.

The library scaffold (runtime adapters, model cache, CLI, REST server,
playground, build and test tooling) comes from ppu-indra-ocr and
ppu-paddle-ocr, Copyright 2025-2026 PT Perkasa Pilar Utama.

The OCRia-nano-1 model files (the ONNX models, their character sets and
metadata) are NOT covered by the Apache License and are not part of this
product. They are the work of LlamaIndex, Inc., distributed under the
